    dest("goa","Goa","Goa","West Coast","Goa",15.2993,74.1240,"4.8",2400,1300,1800,List.of("November","December","January","February"),List.of("beach","nightlife","water-sports","relaxation"),3,6,"Goa rewards slow mornings, beach time and one or two paid water experiences rather than a packed checklist. North Goa suits energy and nightlife, while South Goa is calmer and often better value outside peak weeks.");
    dest("manali","Manali","Himachal Pradesh","Himalayas","Manali",32.2396,77.1887,"4.7",2100,1100,1600,List.of("March","April","May","June","October"),List.of("mountains","adventure","snow","nature"),4,7,"Manali is strongest when the plan leaves weather buffer for mountain roads and altitude. Solang and Old Manali give very different days, so alternating adventure with slow cafe and river time works well.");
    dest("jaipur","Jaipur","Rajasthan","North India","Jaipur",26.9124,75.7873,"4.6",1800,1000,1200,List.of("October","November","February","March"),List.of("heritage","culture","food","shopping"),2,4,"Jaipur is compact enough for efficient sightseeing, with forts in the morning and bazaars after sunset. Start heritage sites early to avoid heat and keep one evening for a food walk.");
    dest("kochi","Kochi (Kerala)","Kerala","South India","Kochi",9.9312,76.2673,"4.6",1700,950,1100,List.of("October","November","December","January","February"),List.of("backwaters","culture","food","relaxation"),2,5,"Kochi blends Fort Kochi heritage, harbour life and easy access to Kerala food and backwater day trips. It is a gentle base for travellers who prefer culture and water over rushing between sights.");
    dest("agra","Agra","Uttar Pradesh","North India","Agra",27.1767,78.0081,"4.4",1500,900,900,List.of("October","November","February","March"),List.of("heritage","monuments","short-trip"),1,3,"Agra is best treated as a focused heritage trip: sunrise at the Taj Mahal, Agra Fort later, and Mehtab Bagh at sunset. It pairs well with Delhi or Jaipur when there are extra days.");
    dest("varanasi","Varanasi","Uttar Pradesh","North India","Varanasi",25.3176,82.9739,"4.5",1300,800,800,List.of("November","December","January","February"),List.of("spiritual","culture","river","food"),2,4,"Varanasi is experienced on foot and by boat: dawn on the Ganges, old-city lanes, Sarnath and the evening aarti. The cheapest days can still feel rich because the riverfront is the main attraction.");
    dest("rishikesh","Rishikesh","Uttarakhand","Himalayas","Rishikesh",30.0869,78.2676,"4.6",1400,850,1300,List.of("September","October","November","March","April"),List.of("adventure","yoga","river","mountains"),2,5,"Rishikesh balances rafting and hikes with yoga and the Ganga Aarti. Keep adventure mornings early and leave afternoons open for cafes, waterfalls and river beaches.");
    dest("udaipur","Udaipur","Rajasthan","North India","Udaipur",24.5854,73.7125,"4.7",1900,1000,1100,List.of("September","October","November","February","March"),List.of("lakes","heritage","romance","culture"),2,4,"Udaipur is a lake city built for unhurried heritage: palaces in the morning, boat rides and rooftop sunsets later. Distances are short, so a well-chosen base saves both money and energy.");
    dest("mysuru","Mysuru","Karnataka","South India","Mysuru",12.2958,76.6394,"4.4",1500,900,900,List.of("October","November","December","January"),List.of("heritage","culture","food","short-trip"),1,3,"Mysuru is an easy-value heritage city: the palace, markets and Chamundi Hills fit comfortably into short trips. It is one of the most forgiving destinations for a tight budget.");
